okf_version: "1.0"
task: "Pre-session provisioning (user: '세션의 시작전에 파일의 준비나 세션을위한 프로그램설치등 스크립트를 준비를 미리 받을수있어서 미리 환경을 프로비전닝할수잇게'; decisions: URL manifest pull, sha256 required, failure blocks the launch, PowerShell + bash + Python; plan approved: '진행'). Survey: docs/journal/2026/10/02/research/provisioning/pre-session-provisioning-survey.okf."
code:
  module: "ciel_runtime_support/remote_provision.py: manifest v1 (files[] {path,url,sha256}, steps[] {id, shell powershell|bash|python, url, sha256, platform windows|linux|macos|any, timeout_s, run once|every_launch}); RemoteProvisioner downloads with the remote-memory rules (http/https incl. redirects, size caps, Authorization only to the manifest origin, %VAR%/${VAR}/{VAR} expansion), places files atomically inside the workspace (unchanged hash -> no download), stores verified scripts as provision/scripts/<sha256>.<ext>, runs them without a shell (powershell.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File | pwsh | bash | ciel's Python) in the workspace with CIEL_WORKSPACE, CIEL_PROVISION_DIR, CIEL_PROVISION_STEP, per-step timeout with process-tree kill, logs provision/logs/<time>-<id>.log, state provision/provision-state.json. provision_before_launch blocks with 'Ciel Runtime launch blocked:' and exit 2. remote_provision_command: 'remote-provision [KEY=VALUE ...] [run] [status]'."
  wiring: "ciel_runtime.sync_remote_launch_assets wraps the existing asset sync with provision_before_launch (every SynchronizedLaunch runtime, reason launch only); remote_provisioner() factory; CliParserRuntime.remote_provision (CliParserSettings is at the 10-field contract cap); config default remote_provision in config_repository. ciel_runtime.py 4980 lines = ratchet budget."
  plan_deviation: "CLI is 'remote-provision run|status' (the repo's KEY=VALUE + bare-action idiom, like 'remote-memory sync') instead of separate 'provision run/status' commands; authorization is one header value like remote-memory, not a headers map."
tests: "tests/test_remote_provision.py 11 tests (manifest validation, disabled, files + once rerun on change, every_launch, sha mismatch never runs, failed step blocks and retries, platform skip, timeout, authorization origin and missing env var, launch block, CLI). Groups: unit 1707 OK (skipped 49), router 1173 OK, channel 448 OK (skipped 80), runtime 344 OK (skipped 19); ruff clean; architecture contracts 261 OK; live router 9611 /health 200."
e2e (Windows, local http.server 127.0.0.1:39555 serving manifest.json / manifest-bad.json, isolated configs, input only via /ca/chat/notify):
  first_launch: "e2e-prov-claude-1790988238: 'Provisioning: file tools/readme.txt written', 'step install-hello ran' (PowerShell wrote bin\\hello.cmd, install-count 1), then my E2E Python step had a syntax error -> 'Ciel Runtime launch blocked: - Provisioning failed: step record-launch exited 1 (log ...)', LAUNCHER-EXIT=2 (screenshot 02-after-turn.png)."
  second_launch: "Same workspace after fixing the E2E script: install-hello skipped (install-count still 1), record-launch ran (launches.txt 19:47:12), Claude Code started (stub provider)."
  cli: "'remote-provision' shows settings; 'remote-provision run status' -> file unchanged, install-hello already done, record-launch ran, complete; status lists both steps with exit 0 and log paths; exit 0."
  bad_hash: "e2e-prov-claude-1790988600 with manifest-bad.json: 'Provisioning failed: sha256 mismatch for step install-hello', LAUNCHER-EXIT=2; no scripts stored, no bin directory (screenshot 01-bad-hash.png)."
  live_session: "e2e-claude-1790988718: CielAiRouter cc/claude-sonnet-5-5, provisioning ran at launch (install-count 1, launches 19:52:01); the session ran the provisioned bin\\hello.cmd and reported 'HELLO-PROVISIONED' (first attempt failed because Git Bash dropped the backslash in the prompt's path, the model retried quoted) (screenshot 01-provisioned-tool.png)."
not_determined: "router.log of a launch starts at the router's 'router_check_state' line; lines the launcher logs before the router starts (including remote_provision_ok/failed at launch) are not in it, while 'remote-provision run' next to a running router is logged. Why the earlier lines are missing was not found; the router child opens the log in append mode. The doc states the state file and step logs as the launch record."
not_verified: "bash and pwsh steps on Linux/macOS were not run on a real Linux/macOS host; the bash and Python command paths are covered by unit tests on Windows (Python executed for real)."
